  <h2 id="pre-and-post-workout-timing">Nutrient Timing: How to Combine Protein and Carbs Around Workouts</h2>

  <p>While total daily macronutrient intake accounts for 80% of your body composition success, strategically pairing protein and carbohydrates around your training session enhances acute recovery and performance:</p>

  <h3>Pre-Workout (1 to 2 Hours Before Training)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Carbohydrates (30g – 60g):</strong> Consume moderate-to-low glycemic carbohydrates (e.g., oats, bananas, sweet potatoes, whole grain toast) to provide sustained bloodstream glucose without digestive distress.</li>
    <li><strong>Protein (20g – 30g):</strong> Include a lean, low-fat protein source (e.g., whey isolate, egg whites, Greek yogurt) to elevate plasma amino acid levels during the workout, blunting muscle breakdown.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Post-Workout (Within 2 Hours After Training)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Protein (25g – 40g):</strong> Ingest a high-quality, leucine-rich protein source to trigger the intracellular mTORC1 pathway and maximize Muscle Protein Synthesis.</li>
    <li><strong>Carbohydrates (40g – 80g):</strong> Consuming fast-digesting carbohydrates replenishes depleted muscle glycogen and triggers an insulin response that aids nutrient delivery into muscle cells.</li>
  </ul>

